    "title": "Unignited Pressure Peaking Phenomena",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4106101",
    "publication_date": "2020-10-19",
    "description": "<ul>\n\t<li>See separate metadata file</li>\n\t<li>The experimental data is provided in three separate parts.</li>\n\t<li>Concentration data from 8 experiments are given in a excel datasheet format with the second and third column as the time and concentration data.</li>\n\t<li>The pressure data is given as text format (ASCII)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Time&nbsp; P1&nbsp;&nbsp; Trigger</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; s&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; kPa&nbsp; V</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The mass flow data is given in text format in the corresponding folder, where CH1 is the time vector, CH2 is the mass flow rate given in Volts. It converts to g/s by mfr = (U-1)*6.25 and CH3 is the pressure at the mass flow meter given in units Volts. It converts to unit bar by p=62.5*(U-1).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Reference paper:&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2020.08.221\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2020.08.221</a></p>",
